OneiOS take18, userland/metal/patches/mesa/0003: Turnip's freed-BO cache gives back BOs no allocation took for 30 s.
Upstream: upstream OneiOS cb32176, userland/metal/turnip-idle-bo-cache.patch (2026-11-24), made for this Mesa; applies with
a 3-line offset (contexts made again: upstream applied it after its trace patch).
What: tu_darwin_bo_cache_trim_idle(age_ms), exported: the cached BOs that sat in the cache for age_ms or longer go back to
the host. Called once a minute with 30000 by userland/metal/Switches.inc's oneios_idle_tick, from NativeMetal 0002's idle
timer (upstream called it from its own row thread, CommandPoolRow.inc).
Why: the cache went back only past its budgets (96 + 16 MiB in the render server, 16 + 8 elsewhere) or at a memory
pressure rise, so a process that went still kept it full (upstream: "tuc 78M" in backboardd at a still screen), every BO
wired guest memory.
Needs: NativeMetal 0002 (the caller's timer). Switch: boot argument oneios-bo-cache-idle=0 (upstream's name): never called.
Removable: yes (ONEIOS_METAL_SKIP=idle-bo-cache-trim). Turnip's build id changes.

